From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:40:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: aop: stop the endpoints for a
 firmware-driven suspend

The AOP keeps running across a sleep. From two traced macOS sleeps on
T8140, and the same order in both, macOS stops its five AFK endpoints
one at a time with 0xa4, each answered by 0x87, then sends the AP power
state as idle. After the wake it sends the AP power state as on, then
starts them again with the existing 0xa3, each answered by 0x86. Nothing
restarts: no HELLO, no ring setup.

So do that in suspend_late, after every child and the sound card have
suspended, and undo it in resume, which also runs if the suspend is
aborted later. A stop or notice that isn't answered within 1 s is undone
and refuses the suspend. No EPIC call starts in between: a call checks
for the sleep again once it holds its turn, so one that waited for it
doesn't slip past the stop. The order is
per-compatible match data, with T8140's taken from the trace. Other SoCs
get endpoint order, and only a firmware-driven suspend reaches any of
this, so s2idle is unchanged.

Whether the AOP's setup port, which macOS's secure side owns, also hears
about the sleep hasn't been traced, so nothing is sent there.

Once the AOP's firmware has crashed it answers nothing, so every later
sleep was refused when its AP idle notice went unanswered. Nothing short
of a reboot restarts it, so a crash RTKit reports leaves the AOP out of
every later sleep and wake: nothing is sent to it, the sleep goes ahead,
and the sensors behind it stay gone until a reboot, as they already
were.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
(cherry picked from commit ca72410da2c055d34e3225c4735b7e01736f1ce6)
(cherry picked from commit a89185207137ba706273e4f4a409b1032efdb02e)
(cherry picked from commit 041b197be8b7e8b9cde93b13fce7a5700ae646fb)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
index 2347073ddc..f6dd325644 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.rs
@@ -3069,6 +3069,50 @@ static AOP_PM_OPS: bindings::dev_pm_ops = bindings::dev_pm_ops {
     ..unsafe { core::mem::zeroed() }
 };
 
+/// The data of a bound AOP device.
+///
+/// # Safety
+///
+/// `dev` is an AOP device between the end of probe and the start of removal.
+unsafe fn aop_from_dev<'a>(dev: *mut bindings::device) -> &'a AopData {
+    // SAFETY: by the caller's contract, drvdata is the `AopDriver` probe set.
+    let driver = unsafe { &*bindings::dev_get_drvdata(dev).cast::<AopDriver>() };
+    let data: *const dyn AOP = &*driver.0;
+    // SAFETY: probe made this `Arc<dyn AOP>` from an `Arc<AopData>`.
+    unsafe { &*data.cast::<AopData>() }
+}
+
+/// # Safety
+///
+/// Called by the PM core with a bound AOP device.
+unsafe extern "C" fn aop_suspend_late(dev: *mut bindings::device) -> c_int {
+    // SAFETY: only reads a flag.
+    if !unsafe { bindings::pm_suspend_via_firmware() } {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    // SAFETY: by this function's contract.
+    match unsafe { aop_from_dev(dev) }.sleep_enter() {
+        Ok(()) => 0,
+        Err(e) => e.to_errno(),
+    }
+}
+
+/// # Safety
+///
+/// Called by the PM core with a bound AOP device.
+unsafe extern "C" fn aop_resume(dev: *mut bindings::device) -> c_int {
+    // SAFETY: by this function's contract.
+    unsafe { aop_from_dev(dev) }.sleep_undo();
+    0
+}
+
+static AOP_PM_OPS: bindings::dev_pm_ops = bindings::dev_pm_ops {
+    suspend_late: Some(aop_suspend_late),
+    resume: Some(aop_resume),
+    // SAFETY: all-zero is a valid `dev_pm_ops`: no callbacks.
+    ..unsafe { core::mem::zeroed() }
+};
+
 kernel::of_device_table!(
     OF_TABLE,
     <AopDriver as platform::Driver>::IdInfo,
-- 
